      "descriptions": [
        {
          "description": "ACRIN 6688, a [18F]-fluorothymidine (FLT) imaging study using positron emission tomography (PET), was designed to evaluate the relationship between [18F] FLT uptake parameters and pathologic complete response to neoadjuvant therapy of the primary tumor in patients with locally advanced breast cancer.Participant Eligibility and Enrollment: Criteria for inclusion were patients with pathologically confirmed breast cancer and determined to be a candidate for primary systemic (neoadjuvant) therapy and for whom surgical resection of residual primary tumor following completion of neoadjuvant therapy is planned. The study was open to enrollment from September 2009 to September 2012. Final accrual to the study was 90 patients, of which 80 were included in the analysis.",
          "descriptionType": "Abstract"
        }
      ],
